Description: sysconfig: report linux-aarch64_ilp32 on AArch64 ILP32
 An AArch64 ILP32 python reported linux-aarch64, and packaging (pip) takes
 linux_aarch64 with 32-bit pointers for 32-bit ARM: its tags became
 linux_armv8l/armv7l, so pip would install AArch32 wheels from PyPI that
 cannot be loaded. With its own platform the tags are linux_aarch64_ilp32
 and any. Only the run-time path changes: cross builds set
 _PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM, which is returned before this code. In 3.13.5 the
 linux branch has an android sub-branch; the check goes into its non-android
 (else) part, so glibc Linux gives "linux-aarch64_ilp32". Same change as
 the OpenWrt 3.13.15 patch 028-sysconfig-aarch64_ilp32-platform.patch.
Author: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no

--- a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
@@ -688,6 +688,11 @@
                 "armv7l": "armeabi_v7a",
             }[machine]
         else:
+            # AArch64 ILP32 (32-bit pointers, AArch64 instructions): its own
+            # platform, so that wheel tags do not take it for 32-bit ARM
+            # (packaging maps linux_aarch64 with 32-bit pointers to armv8l)
+            if machine == "aarch64" and sys.maxsize < 2**32:
+                machine = "aarch64_ilp32"
             # At least on Linux/Intel, 'machine' is the processor --
             # i386, etc.
             # XXX what about Alpha, SPARC, etc?
